IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cpf-rates-and-death`

-- Central Provident Fund Act 1953, First Schedule paras 1 and 7, ss 24(3A) and 25(5) -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_cpf_rates.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

§ `REQ-0001 (cradle-to-grave-simone e041)`

-- Age 23, ordinary wages $4,200, August 2026: 37% = 1,554 total; 20% = 840 from the employee; 714 borne by the employer.
#ASSERT `the total CPF contribution` 23 4200 2026 EQUALS 1554

#ASSERT `the employee's CPF share` 23 4200 2026 EQUALS 840

#ASSERT `the employer's own CPF share` 23 4200 2026 EQUALS 714

